                        ],
                        "form": "overswells"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "6ace65d8-6083-41af-9d51-8bb2c47022b1",
                        "entry_id": "37044c4e-ff39-3925-9a49-8ad4cba5c8aa",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "present"
                        ],
                        "form": "overswelling"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "80e586e7-874e-4ab5-bd63-cb48c81fde73",
                        "entry_id": "37044c4e-ff39-3925-9a49-8ad4cba5c8aa",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "overswelled"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "2195045b-67d5-4a4f-9246-bd5c4ece0fd7",
                        "entry_id": "37044c4e-ff39-3925-9a49-8ad4cba5c8aa",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "overswelled"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "850adea7-05ab-351e-b31a-f2b121b56646",
                        "entry_id": "37044c4e-ff39-3925-9a49-8ad4cba5c8aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To swell or rise above (something, especially the rim of a container, the sides of something hollow, etc.)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "ambitransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "417c1cee-5a45-4b2d-98dc-d2f2581a9b34",
                                "sense_id": "850adea7-05ab-351e-b31a-f2b121b56646",
                                "text": "In some years the river overswells its banks, causing widespread flooding."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e00cb2d-5c88-4695-8aa0-b3cd30ef051f",
                                "sense_id": "850adea7-05ab-351e-b31a-f2b121b56646",
                                "text": "Let floods o’erswell, and fiends for food howl on!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "211ed7fb-3740-405a-a775-429979a89f1a",
                                "sense_id": "850adea7-05ab-351e-b31a-f2b121b56646",
                                "text": "Fill, Lucius, till the wine o’erswell the cup;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea698cdc-682b-414a-9a55-9857ae096ee6",
                                "sense_id": "850adea7-05ab-351e-b31a-f2b121b56646",
                                "text": "Come, you have made mee resolute and bould,\nAnd now receive your lapps ore-swell’d with gold."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "06f5f0b6-a743-41fe-83eb-13fb4651b472",
                                "sense_id": "850adea7-05ab-351e-b31a-f2b121b56646",
                                "text": "1768, Ignatius Sancho, letter to Mr. M—, in Letters of the Late Ignatius Sancho, London: J. Nichols, 3rd edition, 1784, p. 13,\n[…] the heart gratefully throbbing—overswelled with thankful sensations"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5a3d004-28fa-4bea-9d08-3e3c603643b8",
                                "sense_id": "850adea7-05ab-351e-b31a-f2b121b56646",
                                "text": "When mushrooms they were fairy bowers,\nTheir marble pillars over-swelling,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "17bdd4ad-18c4-4138-a8c1-5e8826c8fc98",
                                "sense_id": "850adea7-05ab-351e-b31a-f2b121b56646",
                                "text": "[…] then Badoglio and his staff [went by] looking rather big for their cars, like the necks of bookmakers overswelling their collars;"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "deeb2992-2569-3157-97e0-e4762d1cde7e",
                        "entry_id": "37044c4e-ff39-3925-9a49-8ad4cba5c8aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To cause (something) to be too swollen or large; to become too swollen or large."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "ambitransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "239c73aa-10cd-437c-830d-1af4eb6e4141",
                                "sense_id": "deeb2992-2569-3157-97e0-e4762d1cde7e",
                                "text": "[…] the rents of lands still grew higher upon every lease that expired, till they have arrived at the present exorbitance; when the frog, overswelling himself, burst at last."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "494668f2-8728-41c5-91d0-25693b0f5901",
                                "sense_id": "deeb2992-2569-3157-97e0-e4762d1cde7e",
                                "text": "1885, Richard Burton, The Book of the Thousand Nights and a Night, The Burton Club, Volume 1, Translator’s Foreward, p. xvi,\nMy annotations avoid only one subject, parallels of European folk-lore and fabliaux which, however interesting, would overswell the bulk of a book whose speciality is anthropology."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6314a76d-1860-4d54-bf19-7a56250537bd",
                                "sense_id": "deeb2992-2569-3157-97e0-e4762d1cde7e",
                                "text": "A frequent difficulty in the manufacture of Emmental cheese in America, and perhaps elsewhere, is a tendency for the cheese to overswell."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15ed483a-44a7-4c17-9198-e37b92a662af",
                                "sense_id": "deeb2992-2569-3157-97e0-e4762d1cde7e",
                                "text": "[The monster’s] ungrateful progeny rush to gorge on her blood, but it overswells their bellies and they literally burst to death."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
